Seed the project source closure from configured packages only.

`projectSourcePackagesClosure` took as roots every plan node whose
package id is a project package's, pre-existing nodes included.  Under
cross-compilation a pre-existing package of one machine can share its
package id with a project package of the other: a stable-haskell
`-target` project builds the target's `system-cxx-std-lib-1.0` from
source (as a `packages:` entry), while the build compiler's own
`text-2.1.3` depends on its pre-existing `system-cxx-std-lib-1.0`.  As a
root, that pre-existing unit put every build-machine package above
`text` into the closure (hashable, Cabal-syntax, attoparsec, ...), so
they were planned `-inplace` and rebuilt instead of being reused from
the store -- in a v2 shell, every custom-setup dependency of a project
package.

A project package is always built from source, so only configured
nodes can be roots.  Nothing about unit ids changes for packages that
were not affected.

diff --git a/src/Distribution/Client/ProjectPlanning.hs b/src/Distribution/Client/ProjectPlanning.hs
index 0ab3be567..152844c41 100644
--- a/src/Distribution/Client/ProjectPlanning.hs
+++ b/src/Distribution/Client/ProjectPlanning.hs
@@ -3097,8 +3097,16 @@ elaborateInstallPlan
               -- Take the roots straight from the plan so each 'SolverId' carries
               -- the machine it was solved for; a local package used as a build
               -- tool then contributes both its host and build copies.
+              --
+              -- Only configured packages: a project package is built from its
+              -- source, never taken pre-existing.  A pre-existing package can
+              -- share the package id of a project package on the other
+              -- machine (the build compiler's own @system-cxx-std-lib-1.0@ and
+              -- a project that builds the target's from source), and as a
+              -- root it would put every package built on top of it into the
+              -- closure: inplace, and never reused from the store.
               [ Graph.nodeKey pkg
-              | pkg <- SolverInstallPlan.toList solverPlan
+              | pkg@SolverInstallPlan.Configured{} <- SolverInstallPlan.toList solverPlan
               , isLocalToProject pkg
               ]
 
